<Layout
  title="About Laurens"
  description="Meet Laurens, the person behind Heartbit. Software, curiosity, and making things beyond the screen."
>
  <PageHeading
    eyebrow="02 / THE PERSON"
    title="A person behind every bit."
    description="I’m Laurens. Heartbit is my independent practice for software and making things."
  />
  <section class="content-section prose">
    <h2>From code to something you can hold.</h2><p>
      My work spans software architecture, software engineering, AI engineering,
      and 3D printing. I like moving between the big decisions and the details
      that make an idea work.
    </p><p>
      Some ideas become software. Others end up on a workbench. There’s room
      here for both.
    </p><h2>Why Heartbit?</h2><p>
      A heartbeat tells you something is alive. In software, it can tell you a
      system is still there. A bit is one of the smallest pieces a computer
      works with.
    </p><p>
      Heartbit brings those two ideas together. A small name for the technical
      work and the person behind it.
    </p><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Have a look around the workshop ↗</a>
  </section>
  <section class="contact-strip">
    <h2>Have something in mind?</h2><a class="pixel-button" href="/contact/"
      >Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
    >
  </section>
</Layout>
